# Optional passwords for the three MySQL server accounts created/used by Compose.
# If left unset, Compose uses local-development defaults. The database port is
# bound to 127.0.0.1, so those defaults are intended only for this local setup.
# Set private values here if you need to replace them; never commit the real .env.

# Optional host port for the restricted LAN-only User Web entry point.
# The Windows Agent reports current private IPv4 candidates to Admin for its QR.
# USER_LAN_PORT=8181

# Optional Cloudflare Tunnel connector. Used only by the explicit `tunnel`
# Compose profile. Put the remotely-managed Tunnel token in your ignored local
# .env file; do not put it in Compose commands, source files, or Git.
# Cloudflare's public hostname must target http://gateway-tunnel:8080.
# This origin serves only React User and its allowlisted User APIs; Admin is not
# included in the tunnel image or published through this entry.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# MySQL root administrator. Used by mysql-init only for initial schema/account
# setup (the password is never changed on an existing volume) and by healthcheck.
# The Fastify application and incremental migrator do not connect as root.
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=

# Runtime application account: yukari_app. Fastify uses this for business reads
# and writes (SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE) in the yukari database.
# MYSQL_PASSWORD=

# Read-only inspection account: yukari_viewer. Use it from Navicat to browse
# tables; it has SELECT/SHOW VIEW privileges and is not used by the application.
# MYSQL_VIEWER_PASSWORD=

# Schema-only account: yukari_migrator. Compose uses this for ordered incremental
# DDL migrations; Fastify never uses it. It is provisioned once by mysql-init.
# MYSQL_MIGRATION_PASSWORD=
